# Cloudflare Pages response headers for the embed origin. Copied verbatim into
# embed/dist/ by Vite (this is the project's publicDir).
#
# **This page must stay frameable.** It is framed by Sapling's desktop shell,
# whose document lives at `tauri://localhost` — a custom scheme, and therefore
# an origin no `frame-ancestors` list can name. So there is no
# `X-Frame-Options` here and no `frame-ancestors` anywhere: a policy that tried
# to allowlist the framer would block it instead, which is the failure this
# whole page exists to fix. Cloudflare Pages sets neither header by default;
# this file is the record that the omission is deliberate.
#
# **And no CSP**, for the reason `static/_headers` gives about the app: the page
# loads https://www.youtube.com/iframe_api and frames
# https://www.youtube-nocookie.com, so any policy added later has to name both
# in script-src and frame-src or the player fails with nothing in the console to
# say why. If one is ever added, `frame-ancestors *` has to be part of it.
#
# Being on its own origin is what makes that acceptable: nothing of the
# learner's is here. The page stores nothing, reads nothing, and its whole input
# is an eleven-character video id in the query string.

# Hashed by Vite, so they can be cached forever — same bargain as the app's
# /_app/immutable/*.
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# The page itself is one small document and changes with the app it serves;
# revalidating it every time costs a round trip and buys a fix landing at once.
/youtube.html
  Cache-Control: no-cache
